FLOW1
# f01: the full VS path -> g01 params (fox / marth / battlefield,
# default settings; pre-registration AGENT-LOG iter 88).
# startup runs frames 1-370 (timer transition), then: title -> START ->
# menu-top -> A on VS. MELEE -> menu-battle -> A on LOCAL VS -> css ->
# the TOKEN GESTURE (below) -> START -> sss -> A on battlefield (cursor
# default 0) -> LAUNCH.
#
# RE-AUTHORED for the CSS mechanics arc (docs/MENU-SPEC.md items 1+2+4):
# the row cursor and its L/R stepper are gone, because upstream has no
# value stepper on this screen at all (MENU-SPEC §2.5) — grab-token,
# hover-cell, drop is the ONLY way to choose a character. A flow step is
# now "hold a direction N frames"; FLOW1 already expresses that, since an
# `I` row SETS the held input until the next `I` row, so the format is
# unchanged. The hand moves 2.40 px/frame in x and 3.84 in y
# (DEVIATION D3) on a 240x240 screen.
#
# CLAMP-ANCHORED POSITIONING. Every cursor move here is (a) hold into a
# screen edge until the clamp absorbs the overshoot, then (b) hold a
# counted number of frames away from that edge. The device path drives
# these scripts through a wall-clock injector (flow-to-fkscript.js), so a
# hold can land +/-1 device frame off; anchoring on a clamp makes leg (a)
# exact regardless, and every target below keeps more than one frame of
# slack on each side of leg (b). Positions are the machine's own
# arithmetic, verified against the measured trace.
I 1 -
SHOT 200 startup
SHOT 373 title
I 375 S
I 376 -
SHOT 378 menu-top
I 380 A
I 381 -
SHOT 383 menu-battle
I 385 A
I 386 -
# Anchor: UP x70 clamps y to 0 (the hand starts at y = 224.00, and
# 240/3.84 = 62.5 frames is the whole screen). Then DOWN x12 -> y = 46.08:
# inside the roster band (26,62) with 14 px of slack above and 16 below,
# and inside the cell row (32,62). x is untouched at 28.00, i.e. cell 0
# (6,50) = marth.
I 390 U
I 460 -
I 465 D
I 477 -
# B, rising edge, in the band, P1 is HMN and empty-handed: P1's token is
# retrieved to the hand (css.js:209-215). This also un-readies the screen
# (occupiedToken, css.js:1176).
I 480 B
I 483 -
# Carry RIGHT x38 -> x = 119.20, inside cell 2 (98,142) = fox, crossing
# puff (cell 1) on the way. Hovering a cell SELECTS it live
# (css.js:222-226), so p1char steps 1 then 2 as the token passes.
# The release sits far enough before the drop that the T2 tooth can
# delete it and carry on to cell 3 instead.
I 490 R
I 528 -
# A drops the token on fox and plays its announcer (css.js:263). Deleting
# the release above lets the carry run to here instead (58 frames,
# x = 167.20 = cell 3), which is exactly what the T2 tooth does.
I 548 A
I 551 -
# To port 2's type tab: anchor LEFT+DOWN x105 (clamps x to 0 and y to
# 240), then RIGHT x33 -> x = 79.20 (tab spans 61..97) and UP x36 ->
# y = 101.76 (tab spans 96..107, so this sits 5.76 px above the floor and
# 5.24 below the ceiling — more than one frame of slack either way). The
# clamp is what makes the T2 variant, 48 px further right, converge here.
I 560 LD
I 665 -
I 670 R
I 703 -
I 708 U
I 744 -
# A on the type box runs togglePort(1) (css.js:348-357, main.js:504-520):
# N/A -> HMN. Two non-N/A ports with nothing held is exactly READY TO
# FIGHT (css.js:1167-1181), so START goes live on the next frame.
I 750 A
I 753 -
SHOT 760 css
I 765 S
I 768 -
SHOT 775 sss
I 780 A
I 783 -
END 790
